**nexus-decision-4b** is an open-weight **typed decision model**. You give it an application
state and one or more typed questions (`choice`, `score` or `binary`), each with the options you
allow. For every question it returns one of your options, a **calibrated probability
distribution** over all of them, and a confidence value. It is built for routing, triage,
scoring and gating inside software. It is not a chat model.

It was distilled from **DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash** (the teacher) into **Qwen3.5-4B** (the student)
with LoRA. The training targets were the teacher's soft labels plus its reasoning traces.

## Highlights

- **Accuracy: {{ f3(ci.public.tuned) }}** on {{ "{:,}".format(ci.public.n) }} held-out questions with human labels. That is
  {{ "%+.1f"|format(100 * ci.public.diff) }} points over the untuned base model (95% CI
  {{ "%+.1f"|format(100 * ci.public.diff_ci[0]) }} to {{ "%+.1f"|format(100 * ci.public.diff_ci[1]) }}).
- **More accurate and better calibrated than its teacher on human labels.** Accuracy
  {{ f3(tuned.public.accuracy) }} vs {{ f3(teacher.public.accuracy) }}, ECE {{ f3(tuned.public.ece) }} vs
  {{ f3(teacher.public.ece) }}.
- **Confidence you can threshold.** At confidence ≥ 0.90 it decides {{ pct(thr[0.9].coverage, 0) }} of
  questions with {{ pct(thr[0.9].error) }} error. At ≥ 0.99 it decides {{ pct(thr[0.99].coverage, 0) }}
  with {{ pct(thr[0.99].error) }} error.
- **Stable under option reordering.** Reversing the option order changes
  {{ pct(tuned.all.order_flip_rate) }} of answers, against {{ pct(base.all.order_flip_rate) }} for the base model.
- **Fast.** One forward pass per question, with no generation: {{ "%.0f"|format(lat.l4_fast.p50_ms) }} ms p50 on an
  NVIDIA L4.

| | |
|---|---|
| Parameters | 4B (Qwen3.5 hybrid: Gated DeltaNet + attention; the vision tower is kept from the base) |
| Question types | `choice` (pick one option), `binary` (yes / no), `score` (pick a rubric level) |
| Options per question | 2 to 26 |
| Modes | `fast`: one prefill, no generation (default)<br>`think`: a short `<think>` trace, then the same readout |
| Calibration | One temperature per mode in `nexus_config.json` (fast {{ "%.3f"|format(temps.fast) }}, think {{ "%.3f"|format(temps.think) }}) |
| Languages | Trained mostly on English. Indonesian, Spanish, German, French, Portuguese and Japanese are covered in smaller amounts. |
| License | Apache-2.0 |

