### Think mode

Think mode was evaluated on a random subset of {{ think.n }} test questions:

| Mode | Accuracy (same {{ think.n }} questions) | p50 latency on an L4 |
|---|--:|--:|
| fast | {{ f3(think.fast_accuracy) }} | {{ "%.0f"|format(lat.l4_fast.p50_ms) }} ms |
| think | {{ f3(think.think_accuracy) }} | {{ "%.1f"|format(lat.l4_think.p50_ms / 1000) }} s |

**Think mode does not make decisions more accurate.** It fixes {{ think.think_fixes }} of fast mode's errors but
adds {{ think.think_breaks }} new ones. The two modes agree on {{ pct(think.agreement, 0) }} of questions. Use think mode when
you want a short readable reason (median about {{ "%.0f"|format(think.median_reasoning_chars) }} characters) next to the decision.
For the decision itself, use fast mode.

